The DSP of Guitarix's amp, used by Ikaros Studio's Amp effect: six of its
tube amp models, six tone stacks and its built-in cabinet impulse
responses. Guitarix is GPL 2 or later (COPYING).

  Repository  https://github.com/brummer10/guitarix
  Commit      666b564bb8a7194f200029fdbfbec2abe035f777

Only Faust-generated DSP and the data it needs is kept, unchanged, in
Guitarix's own folder layout:

  src/LV2/faust-generated/gxamp.cc, gxamp5.cc, gxamp7.cc, gxamp8.cc,
      gxamp9.cc, gxamp16.cc                   the tube models
  src/LV2/faust-generated/tonestack_fender_default.cc, tonestack_bassman.cc,
      tonestack_ac30.cc, tonestack_jcm800.cc, tonestack_engl.cc,
      tonestack_ampeg.cc                      the tone stacks
  src/LV2/DSP/valve.h, src/LV2/DSP/tube_tables/*.cc
                                              the tube tables the models use
                                              (the 14 files valve.h includes)
  src/LV2/DSP/cab_data.cc                     the cabinet IRs
  src/LV2/DSP/gx_pluginlv2.h                  the DSP interface

Not used: the LV2 plugin and its GUI (gx_amp.lv2), Guitarix's convolver
(zita-convolver, FFTW) and resampler, and its presence stage (a convolution
in the LV2 plugin, not part of the models). Ikaros convolves the cabinets
with juce::dsp::Convolution and makes presence with a filter; see
src/engine/AmpPlugin.cpp.

ikaros/ is ours: GuitarixAmp.cpp compiles everything above in one file,
inside a namespace of its own, with the few definitions the generated code
expects (see GxFaustSupport.h, shared with external/gxplugins, and the
mydsp_faustpowerN_f helpers from Guitarix's gx_common.h); GuitarixAmp.h is
all the app sees; CMakeLists.txt builds the static library ikaros_guitarix.

To use another model or tone stack: copy its .cc here unchanged, add it to
the enum in ikaros/GuitarixAmp.h and the includes and switch in
ikaros/GuitarixAmp.cpp.
